  "tagline": "The one city in Forsyth County: a county seat whose address reaches 280,000 people, between Lake Lanier and Sawnee Mountain.",
  "summary": "Cumming is the seat of Forsyth County and its only incorporated city. About ten thousand people live inside the city limits; most homes with a Cumming address are outside them, in a county of 280,000 that was a tenth that size in 1980. Georgia 400 made it a commuter county, Lake Lanier is its eastern edge, and its schools rank among Georgia's best. Figures here are Forsyth County's unless they say the city.",
